<!--
  MCU session-slot table config (Round 3278): the SSOT for how many
  sessions one fixed-memory machine holds at once and for the byte ceiling
  of ONE session's slot. SCE emits `SLOT_COUNT` (MAX_SESSIONS) and
  `SLOT_SIZE` (the ceiling), so the RAM every session of the machine may
  take is `SLOT_COUNT * SLOT_SIZE`: one generated number, and the one a deploy
  file's `session_pool: { ref: session_slot_pool_mcu }` is budgeted against
  (`scripts/lib/deploy_sessions.py` documents the keys and checks them).

  ## What a slot is

  The session slot is the storage of one session end to end: the bundle that
  drives it, its link and the socket under it, the engine's staging and the
  fixed tables a peer can fill (aliases, remote declarations, pending replies).
  The table of N of them is the `static` the acceptor claims a slot from BEFORE
  it sends an InitAck, and answers nothing from, counted, when none is free
  (`wz-session-core::session_slot`).

  ## What the two numbers mean

  `slot-count` is MAX_SESSIONS: every session the machine runs, whether it
  dials, accepts or joins a group. The sessions a deploy file declares must fit
  it, and a listening session claims one slot per session it accepts.

  `slot-size` is a CEILING, not a figure derived from a field list. The
  consuming crate asserts, at compile time, that the typed slot is no larger
  than it, so a change that grows the slot past the budget is a build failure
  that names the number to raise. The deploy validator checks the part of the
  ceiling it can see: the pools one session takes (its receive pool and its
  reassembly pool) are part of the slot and so may not add up to more than
  `slot-size`.

  The value is PROVISIONAL, set as the largest pools a declared session takes
  plus room for the typed part: the multicast session of
  `deploy/mcu_client_and_group.yaml` takes 32 x 1536 (the receive pool) +
  4 x 4096 (the reassembly pool) = 65536 bytes, and 32768 more is allowed for
  everything typed. The measured size of the typed slot replaces the headroom
  when the slot owns its socket and its staging (the commit that adds that
  assert moves this number in the same change, with the measurement above it).

  ## What this document does NOT make

  The emitted pool struct (a byte arena of `slot-count` slots and a lifecycle
  FSM) is not instantiated by anything: a second copy of the bytes the typed
  slots take would double the RAM this number budgets. The constants are the
  interface, exactly as the reassembly pool's are for its dispatcher.

  ## section / alignment / cache-policy

  `sram1` / 32 / `none`, as `session_rx_pool_mcu.scxml`. The section is
  advisory (the emit places nothing in it); `none` because no DMA reads a
  session slot, so the C5 cache-maintenance externs stay out of the emit.
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:sce="http://sce.dev/ext"
       sce:kind="buffer-pool" name="session_slot_pool_mcu" version="1.0">
  <sce:slot-count>3</sce:slot-count>
  <sce:slot-size>98304</sce:slot-size>
  <sce:section>sram1</sce:section>
  <sce:alignment>32</sce:alignment>
  <sce:cache-policy>none</sce:cache-policy>
</scxml>
